{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Progress 2026-11-11 (PST): reproduced RED. A stand-in git creates a `.keep`, removes it only on SIGTERM, and spawns a child. Run through `run_git_bounded` with a 1 s bound, it left the `.keep` behind. Fix: `gitutil.run_git(..., timeout=)` now launches through `_run_in_group`, which uses subprocess.run's keywords with its own process group and reaps SIGTERM first via `reap_process_group`. `run_git_reaped` delegates to `run_git_bounded`. 13 existing tests faked `subprocess.run` for bounded git, and each now also patches `gitutil._run_in_group` with the same fake (one line per site). Commit bb29a7b140a in worktree fix-git-kill. make verify is running."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794445563441596908,"uuid":"48880fdc-d397-4bca-b205-31a0cdb43b9a"}